
/*
========================================================
QUESTION 11: REVENUE LEAKAGE ANALYSIS
========================================================

BUSINESS QUESTION:
Quantify billed-to-allowed and allowed-to-collected
financial gaps by insurance payer.

OBJECTIVE:
Identify financial differences between billed charges,
allowed amounts, and actual payments received.

APPROACH:
1. Summarize claims by insurance plan.
2. Summarize payment transactions by insurance plan.
3. Join both summaries using plan_id.
4. Aggregate the results by payer_name to combine plans
   belonging to the same insurance company.
5. Calculate both financial gaps and rank the payers.

========================================================
CTE 1: CLAIM SUMMARY
========================================================

Calculate total claims, billed amounts, allowed amounts,
and claim-recorded payments for each insurance plan.

The LEFT JOIN preserves plans without claims.

Grouping by plan_id and payer_name ensures each plan
has one summarized record before the final analysis.

========================================================
*/

WITH Claim_Summary AS (

    SELECT i.plan_id, i.payer_name,
        COUNT(DISTINCT c.claim_id) AS Total_Claims,
        COALESCE(SUM(c.billed_amount), 0) AS Total_Billed,
        COALESCE(SUM(c.allowed_amount), 0) AS Total_Allowed,
        COALESCE(SUM(c.paid_amount), 0) AS Claim_Recorded_Paid
    FROM insurance_plans i
    LEFT JOIN claims c
        ON i.plan_id = c.plan_id
    GROUP BY i.plan_id, i.payer_name

),

/*
========================================================
CTE 2: PAYMENT SUMMARY
========================================================

Summarize all payment transactions for each plan.

Join using claim_id and patid to associate payments
with the correct claims.

Separating payment aggregation from claim aggregation
prevents multiple transactions from inflating billed
and allowed amounts.

========================================================
*/

Payment_Summary AS (

    SELECT c.plan_id,
        COUNT(DISTINCT p.payment_id) AS Total_Payments,
        COALESCE(SUM(p.amount), 0) AS Total_Payments_Received
    FROM claims c
    LEFT JOIN payments p
        ON c.claim_id = p.claim_id
        AND c.patid = p.patid
    GROUP BY c.plan_id

)

/*
========================================================
FINAL ANALYSIS: PAYER-LEVEL REVENUE LEAKAGE
========================================================

Join both CTEs by plan_id to preserve the correct
relationship between claims and payments.

GROUP BY payer_name combines different insurance
plans belonging to the same payer.

For example, Apex Health Plans 1 and 2 are combined
into one payer-level financial summary.

SUM() combines each plan's financial totals.

COALESCE() treats missing payment summaries as zero.

Billed-to-Allowed Gap:
Total Billed - Total Allowed

Allowed-to-Collected Gap:
Total Allowed - Total Collected

ORDER BY identifies the largest collection gaps first.

========================================================
*/

SELECT s.payer_name,
    SUM(s.Total_Claims) AS Total_Claims,
    SUM(COALESCE(y.Total_Payments, 0)) AS Total_Payments,
    SUM(s.Total_Billed) AS Total_Billed,
    SUM(s.Total_Allowed) AS Total_Allowed,
    SUM(s.Claim_Recorded_Paid) AS Claim_Recorded_Paid,
    SUM(COALESCE(y.Total_Payments_Received, 0)) AS Total_Collected,
    SUM(s.Total_Billed) - SUM(s.Total_Allowed)
        AS Billed_to_Allowed_Gap,
    SUM(s.Total_Allowed) -
        SUM(COALESCE(y.Total_Payments_Received, 0))
        AS Allowed_to_Collected_Gap
FROM Claim_Summary s
LEFT JOIN Payment_Summary y
    ON s.plan_id = y.plan_id
GROUP BY s.payer_name
ORDER BY Allowed_to_Collected_Gap DESC;


